oureteral reflux in patients with self-retaining ureteral stents: implications for upper urinary tract instillation</article-title><source><italic>The Journal of Urology</italic></source><year>2005</year><volume>173</volume><issue>3</issue><fpage>890</fpage><lpage>893</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">15711312</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B11"><label>11</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Miyake</surname><given-names>H</given-names></name><name><surname>Eto</surname><given-names>H</given-names></name><name><surname>Hara</surname><given-names>S</given-names></name><name><surname>Okada</surname><given-names>H</given-names></name><name><surname>Kamidono</surname><given-names>S</given-names></name><name><surname>Hara</surname><given-names>I</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Clinical outcome of bacillus Calmette-Gu&#x000e9;rin perfusion therapy for carcinoma <italic>in situ</italic> of the upper urinary tract</article-title><source><italic>International Journal of Urology</italic></source><year>2003</year><volume>9</volume><issue>12</issue><fpage>677</fpage><lpage>680</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">12492951</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B12"><label>12</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Patel</surname><given-names>A</given-names></name><name><surname>Fuchs</surname><given-names>GJ</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>New techniques for the administration of topical adjuvant therapy after endoscopic ablation of upper urinary tract transitional cell carcinoma</article-title><source><italic>The Journal of Urology</italic></source><year>1998</year><volume>159</volume><issue>1</issue><fpage>71</fpage><lpage>75</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">9400440</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B13"><label>13</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Thalmann</surname><gi